		"ask": "Write `pub fn treynor_ratio(portfolio_return: f64, risk_free_rate: f64, beta: f64) -> f64` (financial: treynor ratio). Calculates the Treynor Ratio for a portfolio. # Inputs - `portfolio_return`: Portfolio return - `risk_free_rate`: Risk-free rate - `beta`: Portfolio beta where Beta is a financial metric that measures the systematic risk of a security or portfolio compared to the overall market. # Output - Returns excess return per unit of market risk",
		"code": "pub fn treynor_ratio(portfolio_return: f64, risk_free_rate: f64, beta: f64) -> f64 {\n    if beta == 0.0 {\n        f64::NAN\n    } else {\n        (portfolio_return - risk_free_rate) / beta\n    }\n}\n",
