		"ask": "Write `pub fn aliquot_sum(number: u64) -> u64` (math: aliquot sum). Aliquot sum of a number is defined as the sum of the proper divisors of a number.\\ i.e. all the divisors of a number apart from the number itself. ## Example: The aliquot sum of 6 is (1 + 2 + 3) = 6, and that of 15 is (1 + 3 + 5) = 9 Wikipedia article on Aliquot Sum: <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aliquot_sum>",
		"code": "pub fn aliquot_sum(number: u64) -> u64 {\n    if number == 0 {\n        panic!(\"Input has to be positive.\")\n    }\n\n    (1..=number / 2).filter(|&d| number.is_multiple_of(d)).sum()\n}\n",
