		"ask": "Write `pub fn softmax(array: Vec<f32>) -> Vec<f32>` (math: softmax). # Softmax Function The `softmax` function computes the softmax values of a given array of f32 numbers. The softmax operation is often used in machine learning for converting a vector of real numbers into a probability distribution. It exponentiates each element in the input array, and then normalizes the results so that they sum to 1. ## Formula For a given input array `x`, the softmax function computes the output `y` as follows: `y_i = e^(x_i) / sum(e^(x_j) for all j)` ## Softmax Function Imple",
		"code": "use std::f32::consts::E;\n\npub fn softmax(array: Vec<f32>) -> Vec<f32> {\n    let mut softmax_array = array;\n\n    for value in &mut softmax_array {\n        *value = E.powf(*value);\n    }\n\n    let sum: f32 = softmax_array.iter().sum();\n\n    for value in &mut softmax_array {\n        *value /= sum;\n    }\n\n    softmax_array\n}\n",
